# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > l+ l- at LO (default coupling orders).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - Drell-Yan over a proton beam with multiparticle labels on both sides: one
#     script is a *group* of concrete subprocesses, which is what exercises the
#     flavour-group path — the per-flavour union of diagrams, the initial-state
#     flavour sum and the PDF luminosity that goes with it.
#   - Default orders here admit both the QED core and the QCD-mediated
#     contributions, so the group's diagram content is the one the order
#     selection chooses rather than one stated by hand; pp_to_ll_qcd0 is the
#     stated-order counterpart, and the pair pins the selection semantics.
#   - Its run is also the hadronic cross-section reference: the two committed
#     dy13 run cards (default cuts, and m_ll in [60,120]) are handed verbatim to
#     both MadGraph and vibegraph, so the PDF luminosity, the flux and the cuts
#     are pinned together rather than one at a time.
#
# Not used for amplitudes: a group has no single matrix element to dump per
# diagram, and the concrete subprocess underneath it — u u~ > mu+ mu- — is a row
# of its own. Per-helicity and per-flow agreement is claimed there, not here.
generate p p > l+ l-
output pp_to_ll -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  done
